// CohRR -- read-read coherence ("Monotonic Increment"), release-acquire.
//
// Source: Arlt & Vafeiadis, "RGSep under Release/Acquire Consistency",
//         PACMPL 10 (OOPSLA2), Article 375, 2026. doi:10.1145/3839507, Section 3.
//
// x is only ever increased, so two reads of it in order never see it decrease:
// the paper proves assert(b >= a) with RGSep and notes it fails under models
// that reorder two reads of one location, such as the Java memory model.
// MoRDor does not implement the JMM; JAM keeps plain accesses coherent.
//
// Reference verdicts:
//   the paper: under RA the assertion b >= a holds, so b < a is forbidden.
//   herd7 7.58 on herd/CohRR.litmus, under the zoo's abstract-sc, abstract-tso,
//     ra, sra, wra and abstract-coherence cat models and herd's rc11.cat:
//     every model forbids.
// The paper's registers are renamed a -> ra, b -> rb:
// MoRDor reads only names beginning with r as registers.
x := 0;
{ ra := x.load(acq); rb := x.load(acq) }
||| { x.store(1, rel); x.store(2, rel) }
%%
forbid (rb < ra) [SC, TSO, RA, SRA, WRA, Coherence, RC11]
